# UNVERIFIED — pending debrief
# Defect 026's own witness, turned into a refusal. Before this, the program
# below compiled, exited 0 and printed `b -> a`: a call made through a function
# VALUE took its arguments by position, because a function type named no
# parameters at any of its sites, and §4.9's rule reads a DECLARATION's names.
#
# `copy_text(from: "a", to: "b")` was refused twice for exactly this. Through a
# value of its own type neither shape was, which is the asymmetry the repair
# removes: the names live in the type now, so the value carries the same rule
# the declaration does, and a relay assignment cannot launder a swap by renaming
# the positions — the names are part of the type's identity.
#
# The fix is `certain` in this direction and only in it: a MISSING label is
# repaired by writing the one the position owns, which leaves every value where
# it is. A label naming another position is the twin case, and its fix is a
# guess (panel 127).
function copy_text(from: str, to: str) -> str
    return from + " -> " + to

function main()
    move: (function(from: str, to: str) -> str) @ copy_text
    print(move(from: "a", to: "b"))  #~ needs_label needs_label
